Changes for IMD, 2026-09-26: combined relevant Lua references into one pinned
REFERENCE.md; added unattended assignment behavior, pixel-art review guidance,
editable-source/export delivery requirements, a manifest, validation conventions
and a dependency-free file checker. Replaced upstream online-reference fetching
and unrestricted-local-script assumptions with the IMD assignment/tool contract.

Aseprite is a separate application. This package includes no Aseprite application,
compiled executable, source archive, application assets or activation credentials.
Operators obtain and install it independently under its own terms. The MCP
connector and this skill do not grant an Aseprite license.

Version 2, 2026-09-26: the advertised capability is pixelart (tool:pixelart).
Aseprite remains the required drawing engine. Operator setup now retains a
separate tested runtime and removes private build materials after verification.

Version 3, 2026-09-26: made STYLE.md an optional reusable art-direction handoff,
with source-grounded documentation when requested, scoped extensions to supplied
